Property.Description:
A package containing one integer entry for each entity ID managed by this PDE.
e.g. Package() {0x1, 0x3, 0x4, 0x15, 0x8, 0x11}
Note- PDEs do not manage other PDEs.

BufferProperty.Description:
This property lists each control that will be affected by when a particular mode is selected. n is encoded as a decimal integer and there shall be one entry for each selected mode. The list of available modes is provided by the mipi-sdca-control-number-range property in the Control Selector Descriptor shown in Table

Contents of the buffer contains data in following format. (need more description here)


Buffer()
{
  0x04,  // Mode Count (1-n)
  0x00,  // Mode 0 (follows)
    0x03,  // Control Count 
      // Entity ID 0 (byte)
      // Control Selector 0 (byte)
      // Control Number 0 (byte)
      // Control Value 0 (4 bytes)
      // Entity ID 1(byte)
      // Control Selector 1 (byte)
      // Control Number 1 (byte)
      // Control Value 1 (4 bytes)
      // Entity ID 2 (byte)
      // Control Selector 2 (byte)
      // Control Number 2 (byte)
      // Control Value 2 (4 bytes)
  0x03,  // Mode 3 (follows)
    0x01,  // Control Count 
...

  0x11,  // Mode 17 (follows)
    0x02,  // Control Count 
...
}
